  "prefLabel": "En 1014.01 Utility Deadlines",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1014.01 Utility Deadlines. The utility shall make reasonable efforts to meet all timelines set by the interconnection procedures. If the utility cannot meet a timeline, the utility shall attempt to notify the applicant in writing in advance of the deadline but in any event no less than one business day after the missed deadline. The notification shall explain the reason for the utility’s failure to meet the deadline and provide an estimate of when the step will be completed. The utility shall keep the applicant updated of any changes in the expected completion date.\n\nSource. #14657, eff 9-1-26, EXPIRES: 9-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html"
